{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mikhail Ilyukhin (born November 21, 1966) is a retired Russian mixed martial artist and professional wrestler who competed in the light heavyweight division.","title":"Mikhail Ilyukhin"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He competed in both RINGS, and Pride Fighting Championships, and was a prominent member of Russia Top Team, where he trained with the likes of Volk Han, Fedor Emelianenko, and Sergei Kharitonov.","title":"Mikhail Ilyukhin"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" At Pride 26, Ilyukhin lost by stoppage to Quinton Jackson.","title":"Mikhail Ilyukhin"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He won his last fight at K-1 – Hero's Lithuania against Jordanas Poskaitis on November 26, 2005.","title":"Mikhail Ilyukhin"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It appears that following the demise of the Russia Top Team Ilyukhin has retired.","title":"Mikhail Ilyukhin"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Art Davie is a business executive and entrepreneur formerly active in Southern California advertising circles.","title":"Art Davie"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" In 1993, he created and co-produced the tournament which became the televised Ultimate Fighting Championship.","title":"Art Davie"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 1998, Davie, as vice-president of K-1 USA, brought the successful K-1 kickboxing franchise from Japan to Las Vegas and North American pay-per-view television.","title":"Art Davie"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In 2003, Davie was an executive producer with Mandalay Sports Entertainment.","title":"Art Davie"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In 2006, he became vice-president of television at Paradigm Entertainment Group.","title":"Art Davie"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In 2014, Ascend Books published Davie's book, "Is This Legal?","title":"Art Davie"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":": The Inside Story of the First UFC from the Man Who Created It".","title":"Art Davie"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Sean Wheelock assisted in the book's research and writing.","title":"Art Davie"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" In November 2014, Davie was inducted into the Legends of MMA Hall of Fame, alongside Big John McCarthy, Pat Miletich, Fedor Emelianenko, and Rickson Gracie.","title":"Art Davie"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Murad Magomedkhanovich Machaev (Russian: Мурад Магомедханович Мачаев ; born December 3, 1986 in Dagestan) is a Russian mixed martial artist of Avar heritage who currently fighting in the lightweight division for the Eurasia Fight Nights Global (EFN), Bellator MMA veteran, he is the winner of the 2011 Fedor Emelianenko Cup.","title":"Murad Machaev"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Antônio Carlos Silva (born September 14, 1979) is a Brazilian mixed martial artist who formerly competed in the heavyweight division of the UFC.","title":"Antônio Silva (fighter)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is a former EliteXC Heavyweight Champion, a former Cage Rage World Heavyweight Champion and a former Cage Warriors Super Heavyweight Champion.","title":"Antônio Silva (fighter)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He has also competed for K-1 Hero's, BodogFIGHT, Strikeforce and World Victory Road.","title":"Antônio Silva (fighter)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Known for being one of the five men (along with Tsuyoshi Kohsaka, Fabrício Werdum, Dan Henderson, and Matt Mitrione) to defeat Fedor Emelianenko in mixed martial arts competition.","title":"Antônio Silva (fighter)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Alexander Vladimirovich Emelianenko (Russian: Александр Владимирович Емельяненко , "Aleksandr Vladimirovich Emel'janenko" ] ; born (1981--) 02, 1981 ) is a Russian mixed martial artist.","title":"Alexander Emelianenko"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is a three-time Russian national Combat Sambo champion and three-time world Combat Sambo champion in the absolute division.","title":"Alexander Emelianenko"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Emelianenko was convicted of aggravated sexual assault in May 2015 and was released early on parole on October 26, 2016.","title":"Alexander Emelianenko"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He is the younger brother of Fedor Emelianenko.","title":"Alexander Emelianenko"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Kirill Yurievich Sidelnikov (Russian: Кирилл Юрьевич Сидельников) born August 17, 1988, is a Russian professional mixed martial artist and grappler, fighting out of Stary Oskol, the same hometown as Fedor Emelianenko with whom he is a training partner.","title":"Kirill Sidelnikov"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He fights for M-1 Mixfight.","title":"Kirill Sidelnikov"}],"peer_messages":["ikhail Ilyukhin"}
